Suppose your university is seeking students’ opinions on whether university libraries should be open to the public. You are now to write an essay to express your view.


###
	Nowadays, university libraries open to the public have arouse generous aruguments. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, university libraries shouldn't 
open to the public, which may bring unpredictable cases.
	For one thing, plenty of strangers that don't be identified have possibility to hit the security of students.  The college students are most of that never experience the society
in person. If school admit the strangers to come in university region, it is unresponsible to the security of students. For another, the public will have influence on students
when students are studying in library. If lots of strangers come to library, nobody can permit them to be quiet.  And they may occupy the learning resources that should be owned 
by students.
	From my perspective, school should ban anybody strange come to school region. Only in this way can make a quiet place to students.


### 逐处错误标注（带序号）
1. university libraries open to the public → whether university libraries should be open to the public 原句主语结构混乱，这是观点类话题，用 whether 从句更合适
2. have arouse → has aroused 时态错误，现在完成时：have/has + 过去分词
3. generous aruguments → general arguments 拼写 + 用词错误；generous 慷慨的，general 普遍的；aruguments→arguments
4. don't be identified → unidentified 形容词 “身份不明的”，语法更简洁地道
5. have possibility to hit the security → may threaten students’ safety 表达生硬；hit security 不成立，threaten safety 表示威胁安全
6. The college students are most of that → Most college students 句式错误，most 直接修饰名词
7. never experience the society in person → have little social experience 地道改写，避免中式表达
8. admit the strangers to come in university region → admit strangers into the campus 固定搭配：admit sb. into…；campus 校园，不用 university region
9. unresponsible → irresponsible 拼写错误
10. will have influence on students → may disturb students disturb 表示打扰，贴合图书馆安静的语境
11. nobody can permit them to be quiet → it is hard to keep quiet 原句逻辑不通，不是没人允许他们安静，而是很难维持安静
12. occupy the learning resources that should be owned by students → take up learning resources which should belong to students take up 占用；belong to 本身表归属，不用被动
13. anybody strange → strangers 形容词修饰名词要前置：strange people /strangers
14. ban anybody strange come to → forbid strangers from entering 固定搭配：forbid sb. from doing sth.
15. Only in this way can make → Only in this way can we create only 倒装句缺少主语，can 后面要接主语


### 修正版
  Nowadays, whether university libraries should be open to the public has aroused general arguments. Opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, university 
libraries shouldn’t be open to the public, which may bring unpredictable problems.
  For one thing, many unidentified strangers may threaten students’ safety. Most college students have little social experience. If the school admits strangers into the campus,
it is irresponsible for students’ safety. For another, the public may disturb students studying in the library. If large numbers of strangers come in, it is hard to keep quiet.
Besides, they may take up learning resources which should belong to students.
  From my perspective, schools should forbid strangers from entering the campus. Only in this way can we create a quiet study environment for students.


### 优化完整版（四级高分，152 词，同立场）
  When it comes to whether university libraries should be open to the public, opinions vary from person to person. As far as I am concerned, it is not a good idea to open 
university libraries to the public.
  For one thing, opening libraries to outsiders may threaten campus safety. Most college students lack enough social experience. Once a large number of unknown visitors enter 
the library, potential safety risks will rise. For another, outsiders may disturb the study order. What’s more, they may occupy seats and books, the limited resources intended 
for students.
  In conclusion, universities should keep libraries mainly for their own students. Only in this way can we guarantee a safe and quiet space for students to study.
